From 45751f36f13522494f040c1c4e7e18fb86df0bee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AOSP RK3576 Baseline <uhf-platform@localbuild>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 10:47:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 06/15] uhf: mark UhfRawTagRecord @VintfStability

Real compiler failure, found by actually running
`m rockchip.uhf.aidl-update-api` again after the previous commit added
this parcelable:

  ERROR: UhfRawTagRecord.aidl:29.11-27: rockchip.uhf.aidl.UhfRawTagRecord
  does not have VINTF level stability (marked @VintfStability), but this
  interface requires it in java

Every type reachable from a `stability: "vintf"` interface - including a
plain data-only parcelable referenced only as an array element type -
must itself declare @VintfStability, so the whole reachable type graph
gets the same stability guarantee. IUhfReader and IUhfReaderCallback
already had it; the new UhfRawTagRecord parcelable just needed the same
annotation added.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 aidl/rockchip/uhf/aidl/UhfRawTagRecord.aidl | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/aidl/rockchip/uhf/aidl/UhfRawTagRecord.aidl b/aidl/rockchip/uhf/aidl/UhfRawTagRecord.aidl
index d96b363..3afedaa 100644
--- a/aidl/rockchip/uhf/aidl/UhfRawTagRecord.aidl
+++ b/aidl/rockchip/uhf/aidl/UhfRawTagRecord.aidl
@@ -26,6 +26,7 @@ package rockchip.uhf.aidl;
  * as legal as an array of any other parcelable regardless of what variable-length data the
  * parcelable itself carries.
  */
+@VintfStability
 parcelable UhfRawTagRecord {
     byte[] data;
 }
